From: reDMP2 <noreply@reexec.local>
Subject: [PATCH] emit: always emit return after tail jump to an import stub

In trampoline mode (--trampoline), emit_static_call_tail() checks is_import()
before is_function() and emits `psp_import_XXXXXXXX();` without a `return;`,
whereas `PSP_TAIL(psp_func_XXXXXXXX);` returns on its own.

The `in.is_jump` emitter site (patched by 0005-emit-trampoline.patch) guarded
its trailing `return;` with `if (!c->trampoline || !is_function(an, in.target))`.
If an import stub address is also present in `an->funcs`, `return;` is omitted
and C control flow falls through into the next label in the function body.

Check `is_import(an, in.target)` so a tail jump to an import stub always emits
`return;`. Other tail-call paths in emit.c either always emit `return;` or
already handle `is_import` before `is_function`.
---
 tools/allegrexrecomp/emit.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/allegrexrecomp/emit.c b/tools/allegrexrecomp/emit.c
--- a/tools/allegrexrecomp/emit.c
+++ b/tools/allegrexrecomp/emit.c
@@ -1079,7 +1079,7 @@ static void emit_function(ectx *c, const a_func *fn) {
                 fprintf(f, "    goto L_%08X;\n", in.target);
             } else {
                 emit_static_call_tail(c, in.target);  /* tail call, and it must stay one */
-                if (!c->trampoline || !is_function(an, in.target))
+                if (!c->trampoline || is_import(an, in.target) || !is_function(an, in.target))
                     fprintf(f, "    return;\n");
             }
             if (have_slot && c->is_label[widx(an, a + 4)]) emit_slot_alias(c, a, &slot, 0);
